.nh
.TH "GUMROAD" "1" "Sep 2026" "Gumroad" "Gumroad CLI"

.SH NAME
gumroad-sales-refund - Refund a sale


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgumroad sales refund  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Refund a sale in full, or partially with --amount.

.PP
--amount is given in the sale's own currency, so by default the sale is looked
up first to find out what that currency is. Without the lookup a value like 25
could mean either $25.00 or ¥25, and sending the wrong one refunds 100 times
the intended amount on a yen-priced sale.

.PP
The lookup needs the view_sales scope in addition to the scope that authorizes
the refund itself. A token issued with only refund permission can skip the
lookup by passing --currency, which is used as-is and trusted without a
server round trip.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--amount\fP=""
	Partial refund amount in the sale's currency (e.g. 5, 5.00)

.PP
\fB--currency\fP=""
	Sale's currency (e.g. usd, jpy); skips the sale lookup, for tokens without view_sales

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for refund


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Enable debug logging to stderr

.PP
\fB--dry-run\fP[=false]
	Preview mutating requests without executing them

.PP
\fB--jq\fP=""
	Filter JSON output with a jq expression

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Output as JSON

.PP
\fB--no-color\fP[=false]
	Disable color output

.PP
\fB--no-image\fP[=false]
	Disable image rendering

.PP
\fB--no-input\fP[=false]
	Disable interactive prompts

.PP
\fB--non-interactive\fP[=false]
	Run in explicit CI/agent mode

.PP
\fB--page-delay\fP=0s
	Wait between paginated --all requests (e.g. 200ms, 1s)

.PP
\fB--plain\fP[=false]
	Output as plain tab-separated text

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Suppress non-essential output

.PP
\fB--yes\fP[=false]
	Skip confirmation prompts


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  gumroad sales refund A-m3CDDC5dlrSdKZp0RFhA==
  gumroad sales refund A-m3CDDC5dlrSdKZp0RFhA== --amount 2.00
  gumroad sales refund A-m3CDDC5dlrSdKZp0RFhA== --amount 25 --currency jpy
.EE


